            Steinmetz,M.O., Guichard,P. and Hamel,V.
  TITLE     WDR90 is a centriolar microtubule wall protein important for
            centriole architecture integrity
  JOURNAL   Elife 9, e57205 (2020)
   PUBMED   32946374
  REMARK    GeneRIF: WDR90 is a centriolar microtubule wall protein important
            for centriole architecture integrity.
REFERENCE   2  (bases 1 to 5540)
  AUTHORS   Valera-Perez,A., Tyrkalska,S.D., Viana,C., Rojas-Fernandez,A.,
            Pelegrin,P., Garcia-Moreno,D., Perez-Oliva,A.B. and Mulero,V.
  TITLE     WDR90 is a new component of the NLRC4 inflammasome involved in
            Salmonella Typhimurium resistance
  JOURNAL   Dev Comp Immunol 100, 103428 (2019)
   PUBMED   31276698
  REMARK    GeneRIF: Study describes WD repeat containing protein 90 (WDR90) as
            a new inflammasome component. Reconstitution experiments of the
            human inflammasome in HEK293cells demonstrated that WDR90 was able
            to physically interact with and to alter the cellular distribution
            of NLRC4, but not of NLRP3 and AIM2.
REFERENCE   3  (bases 1 to 5540)
  AUTHORS   Hamel,V., Steib,E., Hamelin,R., Armand,F., Borgers,S.,
            Fluckiger,I., Busso,C., Olieric,N., Sorzano,C.O.S., Steinmetz,M.O.,
            Guichard,P. and Gonczy,P.
  TITLE     Identification of Chlamydomonas Central Core Centriolar Proteins
            Reveals a Role for Human WDR90 in Ciliogenesis
  JOURNAL   Curr Biol 27 (16), 2486-2498 (2017)
   PUBMED   28781053
  REMARK    GeneRIF: This study identified POB15 and POC16 as two proteins of
            the central core region, the distribution of which correlates with
            that of tubulin glutamylation; POB15 is an inner barrel protein
            within this region. Two poc16 mutants exhibit flagellar defects,
            indicating that POC16 is important for flagellum biogenesis. Human
            WDR90 is required for ciliogenesis, echoing the findings in
            Chlamydomonas.
REFERENCE   4  (bases 1 to 5540)
