   PUBMED   12966086
COMMENT     VALIDATED REFSEQ: This record has undergone validation or
            preliminary review. The reference sequence was derived from
            AC005844.8, AB089940.1, CN400443.1, AK093503.1, AK131277.1 and
            AC006205.9.
            
            On May 17, 2019 this sequence version replaced NM_173593.3.
            
            Summary: B4GALNT3 transfers N-acetylgalactosamine (GalNAc) onto
            glucosyl residues to form N,N-prime-diacetyllactosediamine
            (LacdiNAc, or LDN), a unique terminal structure of cell surface
            N-glycans (Ikehara et al., 2006 [PubMed 16728562]).[supplied by
            OMIM, Aug 2008].
            
